// WW -- the RA-vs-WRA separating behaviour, third shape.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: RA strictly weaker than WRA.
// Source: Lahav & Boker, TOPLAS 2022, Ex. 3.7 (WW).
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/RA-vs-WRA/WW.
//
// Two threads each write x and then read it, and each reads the OTHER thread's
// value. Both writes are hb|loc-unrelated, so WRA's weak-read-coherence -- which
// uses hb|loc rather than mo to decide which of two writes to a location is the
// later -- has nothing to fire on, and WRA allows the outcome. RA and SRA order
// the two writes by mo, so whichever is mo-earlier is read by a thread aware of
// the mo-later one, violating read-coherence. This is WRA failing
// SC-per-location on a single-location program.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA ALLOWS. RA, SRA, C11, RC11 and SC FORBID
//                     (it violates coherence, the zoo's coh column).
//
// Asserted below, by source:
//   herd7 on the zoo's cat models, run on this program: SC forbids, TSO
//     forbids, Coherence forbids, RC11 forbids, RC17 forbids, OD-LSO forbids,
//     RA forbids, SRA forbids, WRA allows.
//   the zoo's equivalence and ordering edges:
//     VbD forbids. Equivalent to SC (zoo edge).
//     x86-TSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     ClightTSO forbids. Equivalent to TSO (zoo edge).
//     RC11z forbids. Equivalent to RC11 (zoo edge).
//     CC allows. Equivalent to WRA on the release-acquire fragment (zoo edge
//       WRA = CC).
//     PC forbids. Coherence forbids it, and PC is stronger.
//   the models' definitions:
//     MW allows. MW alone rejects nothing: a read sees only the write it read.
//   Not asserted, for want of a verdict to check against: MRD, PRAM, Causal,
//     Slow, Local, POCausal, RYW, MR, WFR. C11 and C++17 are not implemented in
//     MoRDor.
x := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel);
  r0 := x.load(acq)
} ||| {
  x.store(2, rel);
  r1 := x.load(acq)
}
%%
allow (r0 = 2 && r1 = 1) [WRA, CC, MW]
forbid (r0 = 2 && r1 = 1) [SC, VbD, TSO, x86-TSO, ClightTSO, Coherence, RC11,
                           RC11z, RC17, OD-LSO, RA, SRA, PC]
